; Leg GQ -- the host SENDS.  CKERMITW (shipping, WITH section 1f)
; RECEIVES 32 KB at 38400.  RUN IMMEDIATELY AFTER GP.
;
; GQ minus GP is the cost of section 1f: four instructions per byte in the
; ISR, about five on the polled transmit path, +1,530 bytes of image and
; +32 of DGROUP.  SS16w says code size is execution time on an 8088, so the
; size is part of the cost and not a confound.
;
; If GQ - GP is near zero, SS16ak's +11% was two sittings and not a change,
; and the figure should be withdrawn.  If it is near 3 s, section 1f costs
; 11% of a 38400 receive and that is a fact the port has to decide about.
set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set retry 30
set parity none
set flow none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16alGQ.pkt
send rcvgq.dat
statistics
